Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["InfraRadarChart", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"a9936d07-838a-4c9c-b0be-70b7e71e437c"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraRadarChart"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/InfraRadarChart", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36309149-d22f-42d3-a307-146aa342fa9d"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is the radar chart of the observer ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ": it gives every event between the first and the last tick of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " its radar time and radar distance.",
 "\n",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"4046b779-e7ae-4f5d-8788-9f5722f41ff9"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraRadarChart"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/InfraRadarChart", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", " ", 
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], ",", " ", "\[Ellipsis]"}], "}"}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a6e6aa4c-2c8c-4058-83fb-8dc3dadd274d"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "joins the radar charts of several observers on the events they all chart."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"70d6b823-583d-45f4-8965-5584913f6ef7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: for an observer ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " = (",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 "1 \[Precedes] ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 "2 \[Precedes] \[Ellipsis] \[Precedes] ",
 StyleBox["ak", "TI"],
 "), a chain given as a vertex list in causal order, and an event ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 " of the radar domain [",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 "1, ",
 StyleBox["ak", "TI"],
 "], the emission tick is ",
 StyleBox["i", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 ") = max{",
 StyleBox["i", "TI"],
 " : ",
 StyleBox["ai", "TI"],
 " \[PrecedesSlantEqual] ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 "}, the latest tick that can signal ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 ", and the reception tick is ",
 StyleBox["j", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 ") = min{",
 StyleBox["j", "TI"],
 " : ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 " \[PrecedesSlantEqual] ",
 StyleBox["aj", "TI"],
 "}, the earliest tick ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 " can signal. The radar time of ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 " is (",
 StyleBox["i", "TI"],
 " + ",
 StyleBox["j", "TI"],
 ")/2 and its radar distance (",
 StyleBox["j", "TI"],
 " \[Minus] ",
 StyleBox["i", "TI"],
 ")/2."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"72660926-6320-4f59-aec0-e7f0d3d1cbb5"],

Cell["\<\
This is the radar construction of special relativity, made with the ticks of \
a clock instead of the readings of a continuous one: an event on the observer \
is its own emission and reception, at distance 0 and at its own tick; an \
event off it is seen by the latest signal that can reach it and answers the \
earliest signal it can send. Radar time is weakly monotone along every edge \
and radar distance is never negative. Radar distance is unsigned, so a single \
observer cannot tell left from right: the chart of a symmetric observer folds \
the graph along it. Joining the charts of several observers separates what \
one of them identifies.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"96ddd2c6-57c8-427e-b2bb-914b24e63e64"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The head holds its observers and computes nothing. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d7d37c28-f132-4907-88e7-a7d0c0a93668"],
 " reads it on a graph:"
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"1c5e1359-9d3c-4910-a886-c2e3dea97ffa"],

